      "id": "Q4",
      "text": "Where possessory relief does not determine ownership and the competing title question is expressly reserved, the parties remain able to seek adjudication of their competing titles in duly constituted proceedings. A claimant seeking title-based eviction must first establish the better right to possession.",
      "submitted_text": "Because possession-based protection does not determine ownership, the Supreme Court expressly reserved title, and E2 had not established the title needed to justify eviction in the reviewed proceedings, the parties may pursue competing proprietary claims in duly constituted proceedings. E2's prospective title-based eviction depends on establishing a better right to possession. The conclusion does not establish any present right of self-help eviction or predict the result of future litigation.",
